& [TerminalCorrelationShape] is caught from generated official schemas
  + [observation] is item notifications use params.turnId while turn/completed uses params.turn.id
  + [repair] is distinct exact correlation validators and a negative terminal-substitution test
  + [status] is resolved

& [CommentaryFinalDistinction] is caught before live activation
  + [observation] is completed agent messages may be commentary or final_answer and legacy providers may omit phase
  + [repair] is treat commentary as passive and allow exactly one final or legacy-phase message only after the exact tool completion
  + [status] is resolved

& [ProofReferenceForgery] is found during post-compile trust review
  + [risk] is an untrusted model could name a syntactically valid proof identity and satisfy the mechanical Observer presence check
  + [repair] is the supervisor supplies the exact admitted proof set, the prompt declares it, and the adapter requires set equality
  + [proof] is the model-invented proof integration test
  + [status] is resolved

& [UnboundedLineAllocation] is found during transport review
  + [risk] is checking line length only after `read_until` can allocate beyond the configured line budget
  + [repair] is wrap each read with a maximum-plus-one `Take` before allocation and fault on the first excess byte
  + [status] is resolved

& [StrictSchemaUniqueItems] is caught by a real provider response
  + [observation] is the model API rejects `uniqueItems` in the strict response schema
  + [repair] is emit the supported array schema and independently reject duplicate strings before deserializing to ordered sets
  + [proof] is duplicate-set parser test plus successful live schema admission
  + [status] is resolved

& [OutdatedCodexVersion] is caught by the first live model request
  + [observation] is pinned codex-cli 0.135.0 is rejected for configured gpt-5.6-sol because a newer Codex is required
  + [repair] is install official codex-cli 0.146.0 under ignored project-local runtime and regenerate exact path, version, and digest pins
  + [global_effect] is none; the global Codex installation was not modified
  + [status] is resolved_for_probe

& [PassiveNotificationCoverage] is caught by live event admission
  + [observations] are warning and thread/status/changed notifications before model completion
  + [repair] is allow bounded official passive notifications, retain advisories as evidence, and keep `error` as an immediate typed fault with bounded detail
  + [status] is resolved

& [MissingToolLiveTurns] is observed twice on finalized candidate-binding code
  + [observation] is the model produced a final response before the required Cantor call
  + [correct_behavior] is the adapter faulted at assigned progress and admitted no query, response, or candidate
  + [repair] is add a concise thread developer instruction in addition to the assignment primer
  + [retry_boundary] is no automatic retry exists; the later positive probe was a separately invoked operator cycle
  + [status] is fail_closed_with_nondeterminism_visible

& [CandidateEvidenceBinding] is strengthened after live success review
  + [risk] is a driver could supply candidate structure and evidence digests that do not bind the exact final message
  + [repair] is retain final message, reparse it, compare the parsed candidate, independently recompute three digests, and bind candidate identity to turn plus message digest
  + [status] is resolved

& [ToolMaskingBoundary] is documented rather than overstated
  + [observation] is stable App Server exposes built-in Codex capabilities in addition to configured MCP while this profile supplies read-only no-network sandbox and forbids every other started item
  + [limit] is a forbidden read-only built-in action can begin before its started event reaches the client
  + [resolution] is terminate at the first observable event and make no claim of provider-side pre-inference tool masking
  + [status] is bounded_nonclaim

& [EvidenceStaleness] is expected at global release gate
  + [observation] is existing clone-portable manifests reject changed Cargo.lock and shared navigation files
  + [repair] is complete all shared surfaces then regenerate prerequisite manifests in dependency order before the new live manifest
  + [status] is pending_final_release_gate

& [UnboundedStdoutQueue] is found during post-proof resource audit
  + [risk] is the reader can queue lines faster than consumer-side total-byte accounting
  + [repair] is replace the unbounded channel with a synchronous two-line queue
  + [status] is resolved_and_live_reproved

& [BoundedStderrDeadlock] is found during post-proof resource audit
  + [risk] is stopping stderr reads at the retention cap can fill the child pipe and deadlock progress
  + [repair] is continue draining to EOF while retaining at most the bounded prefix
  + [status] is resolved_and_live_reproved

& [PartialSpawnAndExitAccounting] is found during child-ownership audit
  + [risk] is a rare missing pipe can leave a spawned process and a completed turn can hide forced or nonzero termination
  + [repair] is exact-child terminate-and-wait for partial setup plus graceful successful exit as the only accepted normal completion
  + [status] is resolved_and_live_reproved

& [ReturnedThreadAuthority] is found during response audit
  + [risk] is accepting only ephemeral identity does not prove returned approval, sandbox, network, and cwd match the request
  + [repair] is exact returned-authority validation and negative workspace-write substitution test
  + [status] is resolved_and_live_reproved

& [PreResponseNotificationAdmission] is narrowed
  + [risk] is accepting arbitrary notification-shaped values before a response can hide interface drift
  + [repair] is a phase-specific allowlist; current remoteControl/status/changed was discovered live and explicitly admitted as passive
  + [status] is resolved_and_live_reproved
